  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Africa Virtual Investment Platform (AVIP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The African Virtual Investment Platform (AVIP) aims to address critical barriers to investment in Africa by providing comprehensive, timely, and reliable data on the continent&apos;s investment landscape. AVIP is a cornerstone of the Africa-OECD Partnership, endorsed by the OECD Ministerial Council in June 2023, and aligned with strategic frameworks such as Agenda 2063 and the African Continental Free Trade Area (AfCFTA). &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Overall Objective is to accelerate the mobilisation of public and private investment for Africa&#xbf;s productive transformation, job creation and sustainable development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Specific Objective (Outcome) is is to develop comprehensive and reliable data and analysis on Africa&#xbf;s investment landscape and improve investment data collection and policy-making on the African continent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;AVIP&#xbf;s implementation will contribute to three main outputs:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;&lt;em&gt;Comparable data, indicators and granular analysis on investment trends and policies in Africa are developed:&lt;/em&gt; AVIP will provide regularly updated indicators and analysis of Africa&#xbf;s investment landscape, covering foreign and domestic investment trends, infrastructure ecosystems, and sustainability impacts. A user-friendly online portal will serve as a central repository for this data, enabling tailored visualisations and country-specific profiles.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;&lt;em&gt;The capacity of national, regional, and continental African statistical and other institutions to collect investment data and engage in investment impact and policy analysis is developed. : &lt;/em&gt;Through targeted training and technical support, AVIP will strengthen the capabilities of African statistical agencies and investment promotion entities to collect, harmonise, and analyse investment data. This capacity-building effort ensures long-term ownership and sustainability of the platform.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;&lt;em&gt;Global, regional and national policy dialogue and cooperation on investment policies and good practices in view of implementing AU investment priorities, including the AfCFTA Investment Protocol, is enhanced. : &lt;/em&gt;AVIP will facilitate structured dialogues between public and private stakeholders, focusing on investment climate reforms and regional integration. These efforts aim to align national policies with the AfCFTA Investment Protocol and other global standards, such as the World Trade Organization (WTO) Investment Facilitation for Development, as well as contributing to the implementation of Sustainable Investment Facilitation Agreement negotiated by the European Union (EU), fostering an enabling environment for sustainable investments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
